---
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Simulate it" hint="Shortest-path algorithms on graphs from fixed formulas, with steps counted instead of time. A step is one comparison inside the heap, one node looked at while scanning for the closest one, or one edge checked. The same graph always gives the same numbers. The adversarial graph at 1,000 nodes does about 18 million steps and takes a second to compute.">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>Set <b>Graph</b> to <b>Sparse (3 edges per node)</b> and <b>Nodes</b> to <b>1,000</b>: with <b>3,000</b> edges, Dijkstra with an array scans for the closest node every time and needs <b>602,800</b> steps; with a heap it needs <b>9,557</b>, with <b>657</b> pushes.</li>
    <li>Set <b>Graph</b> to <b>Dense, every edge improves</b>: <b>499,500</b> edges, and now the heap needs <b>18,148,855</b> steps against <b>1,500,500</b> for the array, because every relaxation pushes a new entry (<b>499,501</b> pushes). Set <b>Graph</b> to <b>Dense (half of the nodes)</b> and the heap wins again: <b>266,979</b> against <b>752,000</b>, since most relaxations push nothing.</li>
    <li>In <b>Negative weights</b>, with <b>Nodes</b> at <b>1,000</b>: Bellman-Ford makes <b>5,988</b> edge checks, while Dijkstra is wrong for <b>992</b> of the 1,000 nodes, too long by up to <b>199</b>, and reports no error. In <b>Bellman-Ford's worst case</b>, a chain whose edges point against the sweep order needs <b>500,499</b> edge checks in <b>1,000</b> rounds, where Dijkstra needs <b>999</b>.</li>
    <li>In <b>A* on a grid</b>, set <b>Grid size</b> to <b>100 x 100</b> and <b>Heuristic</b> to <b>Manhattan distance</b>: A* expands <b>652</b> nodes where Dijkstra expands <b>9,092</b>, and both find a path of cost <b>198</b>. Set <b>Heuristic</b> to <b>3 x Manhattan distance</b>: only <b>211</b> expansions, but the path costs <b>210</b>, not the shortest.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg sp" data-sp>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Graph <select class="pg-in" data-kind><option value="sparse" selected>Sparse (3 edges per node)</option><option value="dense">Dense (half of the nodes)</option><option value="adversarial">Dense, every edge improves</option></select></label>
      <label>Nodes <select class="pg-in" data-v><option value="100">100</option><option value="500">500</option><option value="1000" selected>1,000</option></select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Dijkstra: array or heap?</h3>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>Edges</h3><span class="pg-mono sp-big" data-e></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" data-ab><h3>Array: scan for the closest node</h3><span class="pg-mono sp-big" data-a></span><span class="pg-note">V steps per scan, one scan per settled node, plus the edge checks</span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" data-hb><h3>Binary heap</h3><span class="pg-mono sp-big" data-h></span><span class="pg-note" data-hn></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>Winner</h3><span class="pg-mono sp-big" data-w></span><span class="pg-note" data-wn></span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sp-bars" data-bars></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Negative weights</h3>
      <p class="pg-note">A layered graph with edges only going forward and weights from -4 to 10: no cycles, so shortest paths exist. Dijkstra settles each node once; Bellman-Ford sweeps all edges until nothing improves.</p>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--good)"><h3>Bellman-Ford</h3><span class="pg-mono sp-big" data-n1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1n></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" data-nb2><h3>Dijkstra</h3><span class="pg-mono sp-big" data-n2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2n></span></div>
      </div>
      <span class="pg-note" data-ex></span>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>Bellman-Ford's worst case</h3>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>Sparse graph, positive weights</h3><span class="pg-mono sp-big" data-f1></span><span class="pg-note" data-f1n></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" data-fb2><h3>Chain against the sweep order</h3><span class="pg-mono sp-big" data-f2></span><span class="pg-note" data-f2n></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)">
      <h3>A* on a grid</h3>
      <div class="pg-row">
        <label>Grid size <select class="pg-in" data-grid><option value="20">20 x 20</option><option value="50">50 x 50</option><option value="100" selected>100 x 100</option></select></label>
        <label>Heuristic <select class="pg-in" data-heur><option value="1" selected>Manhattan distance</option><option value="3">3 x Manhattan distance</option><option value="0">None (this is Dijkstra)</option></select></label>
      </div>
      <p class="pg-note">Start in one corner, goal in the opposite one, every move costs 1 and some cells are blocked. The heuristic estimates the distance left; priority is cost so far plus that estimate.</p>
      <div class="pg-grid">
        <div class="pg-box" style="--c: var(--border)"><h3>Dijkstra expands</h3><span class="pg-mono sp-big" data-s1></span><span class="pg-note" data-s1n></span></div>
        <div class="pg-box" data-sb2><h3>With the chosen heuristic</h3><span class="pg-mono sp-big" data-s2></span><span class="pg-note" data-s2n></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, formatThousands } from '../playground';

  // The same model as the code samples, ported to TypeScript.
  const INF = 1000000000, KEY = 100000, OFFSET = 1000000, TIE = 4096;
  class Heap {
    a: number[] = []; c = 0;
    push(key: number) {
      const a = this.a; a.push(key); let i = a.length - 1;
      while (i > 0) { const p = Math.floor((i - 1) / 2); this.c++; if (key < a[p]) { a[i] = a[p]; i = p; } else break; }
      a[i] = key;
    }
    pop(): number {
      const a = this.a, top = a[0], last = a.pop()!;
      if (a.length > 0) {
        const n = a.length; let i = 0;
        for (;;) {
          let s = 2 * i + 1; if (s >= n) break;
          if (s + 1 < n) { this.c++; if (a[s + 1] < a[s]) s++; }
          this.c++;
          if (a[s] < last) { a[i] = a[s]; i = s; } else break;
        }
        a[i] = last;
      }
      return top;
    }
  }
  type Graph = [number, number][][];
  function makeGraph(kind: string, v: number): Graph {
    const adj: Graph = Array.from({ length: v }, () => []);
    for (let i = 0; i < v; i++) {
      if (kind === 'sparse') {
        for (let k = 0; k < 3; k++) { let t = (i * (2 * k + 3) * 7919 + k * 104729 + 13) % v; if (t === i) t = (t + 1) % v; adj[i].push([t, 1 + ((i * 31 + k * 17 + t * 7) % 20)]); }
      } else if (kind === 'dense') {
        for (let k = 0; k < Math.floor(v / 2); k++) { const t = (i + 1 + 2 * k + (i % 2)) % v; if (t !== i) adj[i].push([t, 1 + ((i * 31 + t * 17) % 20)]); }
      } else if (kind === 'adversarial') {
        for (let t = i + 1; t < v; t++) adj[i].push([t, t === i + 1 ? 1 : 3 * (v - i) + (t - i)]);
      } else if (kind === 'backward') {
        if (i > 0) adj[i].push([i - 1, 1]);
      } else {
        for (let t = i + 1; t < Math.min(v, i + 4); t++) adj[i].push([t, ((i * 37 + t * 11) % 15) - 4]);
      }
    }
    return adj;
  }
  function dijkstraArray(adj: Graph, src: number): [number[], number] {
    const v = adj.length, dist = new Array<number>(v).fill(INF), done = new Array<boolean>(v).fill(false);
    dist[src] = 0; let steps = 0;
    for (;;) {
      let best = -1;
      for (let u = 0; u < v; u++) { steps++; if (!done[u] && dist[u] < INF && (best < 0 || dist[u] < dist[best])) best = u; }
      if (best < 0) break;
      done[best] = true;
      for (const [t, w] of adj[best]) { steps++; if (dist[best] + w < dist[t]) dist[t] = dist[best] + w; }
    }
    return [dist, steps];
  }
  function dijkstraHeap(adj: Graph, src: number): [number[], number, number] {
    const v = adj.length, dist = new Array<number>(v).fill(INF), done = new Array<boolean>(v).fill(false);
    dist[src] = 0; const h = new Heap(); let edges = 0, pushes = 1;
    h.push(OFFSET * KEY + src);
    while (h.a.length > 0) {
      const u = h.pop() % KEY;
      if (done[u]) continue;
      done[u] = true;
      for (const [t, w] of adj[u]) { edges++; if (dist[u] + w < dist[t]) { dist[t] = dist[u] + w; h.push((dist[t] + OFFSET) * KEY + t); pushes++; } }
    }
    return [dist, h.c + edges, pushes];
  }
  function bellmanFord(adj: Graph, src: number): [number[], number, number] {
    const v = adj.length, dist = new Array<number>(v).fill(INF); dist[src] = 0; let relax = 0, rounds = 0;
    for (let r = 0; r < v; r++) {
      let changed = false; rounds++;
      for (let u = 0; u < v; u++) { if (dist[u] === INF) continue; for (const [t, w] of adj[u]) { relax++; if (dist[u] + w < dist[t]) { dist[t] = dist[u] + w; changed = true; } } }
      if (!changed) break;
    }
    return [dist, relax, rounds];
  }
  const edgeCount = (adj: Graph) => adj.reduce((s, x) => s + x.length, 0);
  const gridOpen = (w: number, x: number, y: number) => ((x === 0 && y === 0) || (x === w - 1 && y === w - 1)) ? true : (x * 31 + y * 17) % 11 !== 0;
  function aStar(w: number, factor: number): [number, number] {
    const n = w * w, goal = n - 1, g = new Array<number>(n).fill(INF), closed = new Array<boolean>(n).fill(false);
    g[0] = 0; const h = new Heap(); let expanded = 0;
    h.push(factor * (2 * (w - 1)) * TIE * KEY);
    while (h.a.length > 0) {
      const u = h.pop() % KEY;
      if (closed[u]) continue;
      closed[u] = true; expanded++;
      if (u === goal) return [expanded, g[u]];
      const x = u % w, y = Math.floor(u / w);
      for (const [nx, ny] of [[x + 1, y], [x, y + 1], [x - 1, y], [x, y - 1]]) {
        if (nx >= 0 && nx < w && ny >= 0 && ny < w && gridOpen(w, nx, ny)) {
          const t = ny * w + nx;
          if (g[u] + 1 < g[t]) { g[t] = g[u] + 1; h.push(((g[t] + factor * ((w - 1 - nx) + (w - 1 - ny))) * TIE - g[t]) * KEY + t); }
        }
      }
    }
    return [expanded, -1];
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-sp]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const colour = (id: string, c: string) => q<HTMLElement>(id).style.setProperty('--c', c);
    const sel = (s: string) => q<HTMLSelectElement>(s).value;
    const cache = new Map<string, any>();
    const memo = <T,>(key: string, f: () => T): T => { if (!cache.has(key)) cache.set(key, f()); return cache.get(key); };
    function draw() {
      const kind = sel('[data-kind]'), v = Number(sel('[data-v]'));
      const r = memo(`h${kind}/${v}`, () => {
        const adj = makeGraph(kind, v);
        return { e: edgeCount(adj), a: dijkstraArray(adj, 0)[1], h: dijkstraHeap(adj, 0) };
      });
      q('[data-e]').textContent = formatThousands(r.e);
      q('[data-a]').textContent = formatThousands(r.a);
      q('[data-h]').textContent = formatThousands(r.h[1]);
      q('[data-hn]').textContent = `${formatThousands(r.h[2])} pushes: every push costs comparisons to climb`;
      const heapWins = r.h[1] < r.a;
      q('[data-w]').textContent = heapWins ? 'Heap' : 'Array';
      const ratio = heapWins ? r.a / r.h[1] : r.h[1] / r.a;
      q('[data-wn]').textContent = `${ratio >= 10 ? formatThousands(Math.round(ratio)) : Math.round(ratio * 10) / 10}x fewer steps. ${heapWins ? 'The heap helps when the graph is sparse or most relaxations push nothing.' : 'Here nearly every edge improves a distance, so the heap pays log V for each of them while the array pays a flat V per node.'}`;
      colour('[data-ab]', heapWins ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      colour('[data-hb]', heapWins ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
      const bars = q('[data-bars]'); bars.textContent = '';
      const rows: [string, number][] = [['Array', r.a], ['Binary heap', r.h[1]]];
      const top = Math.log10(Math.max(...rows.map((x) => x[1]), 10));
      for (const [label, val] of rows) {
        const row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'sp-bar';
        const name = document.createElement('span'); name.textContent = label;
        const track = document.createElement('span'); track.className = 'sp-track';
        const fill = document.createElement('span'); fill.className = 'sp-fill'; fill.style.width = `${Math.max(2, (Math.log10(Math.max(1, val)) / top) * 100)}%`;
        track.appendChild(fill); row.append(name, track); bars.appendChild(row);
      }

      const n = memo(`n${v}`, () => {
        const adj = makeGraph('negative', v);
        const [bf, relax, rounds] = bellmanFord(adj, 0), [dj, steps] = dijkstraHeap(adj, 0);
        let wrong = 0, worst = 0;
        for (let i = 0; i < v; i++) { if (bf[i] !== dj[i]) wrong++; worst = Math.max(worst, dj[i] - bf[i]); }
        return { relax, rounds, steps, wrong, worst };
      });
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = `${formatThousands(n.relax)} edge checks`;
      q('[data-n1n]').textContent = `${formatThousands(n.rounds)} rounds: stops when a sweep changes nothing; correct with negative edges`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = `wrong for ${formatThousands(n.wrong)} of ${formatThousands(v)} nodes`;
      q('[data-n2n]').textContent = `too long by up to ${formatThousands(n.worst)}, after ${formatThousands(n.steps)} steps and no error: a settled node is never revisited, but a later negative edge can still lower its distance`;
      colour('[data-nb2]', n.wrong > 0 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      const tri: Graph = [[[1, 3], [2, 5]], [[3, 1]], [[1, -4]], []];
      const dt = dijkstraHeap(tri, 0)[0], bt = bellmanFord(tri, 0)[0];
      q('[data-ex]').textContent = `Four nodes, A to B costs 3, A to C costs 5, C to B costs -4, B to D costs 1: Dijkstra says D costs ${dt[3]}, Bellman-Ford says ${bt[3]}. Dijkstra had already settled B (at 3) and passed that distance on to D before the cheaper way through C was found.`;

      const f = memo(`f${v}`, () => {
        const sp = makeGraph('sparse', v), bk = makeGraph('backward', v);
        const [, r1, k1] = bellmanFord(sp, 0), [, s1] = dijkstraHeap(sp, 0);
        const [, r2, k2] = bellmanFord(bk, v - 1), [, s2] = dijkstraHeap(bk, v - 1);
        return { r1, k1, s1, r2, k2, s2 };
      });
      q('[data-f1]').textContent = `${formatThousands(f.r1)} edge checks`;
      q('[data-f1n]').textContent = `${formatThousands(f.k1)} rounds; Dijkstra with a heap needs ${formatThousands(f.s1)} steps`;
      q('[data-f2]').textContent = `${formatThousands(f.r2)} edge checks`;
      q('[data-f2n]').textContent = `${formatThousands(f.k2)} rounds: the news travels one hop per sweep, so the cost approaches V times E; Dijkstra needs ${formatThousands(f.s2)} steps`;
      colour('[data-fb2]', f.r2 > 10 * f.s2 ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--border)');

      const w = Number(sel('[data-grid]')), factor = Number(sel('[data-heur]'));
      const base = memo(`a${w}/0`, () => aStar(w, 0)), mine = memo(`a${w}/${factor}`, () => aStar(w, factor));
      q('[data-s1]').textContent = `${formatThousands(base[0])} nodes`;
      q('[data-s1n]').textContent = `of ${formatThousands(w * w)} cells; shortest path cost ${formatThousands(base[1])}`;
      q('[data-s2]').textContent = `${formatThousands(mine[0])} nodes`;
      q('[data-s2n]').textContent = `path cost ${formatThousands(mine[1])}. ${mine[1] === base[1] ? (factor === 0 ? 'No heuristic: the same as Dijkstra.' : 'The same cost as Dijkstra: the heuristic never overestimates, so the path is still the shortest.') : `Longer than the shortest (${formatThousands(base[1])}): the heuristic overestimates the distance left, so A* stops sooner with a worse path.`}`;
      colour('[data-sb2]', mine[1] === base[1] ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)');
    }
    root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
<style is:global>
  .playground .sp-big { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .playground .sp-bars { display: grid; gap: 6px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .playground .sp-bar { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr; gap: 2px 8px; align-items: center; }
  .playground .sp-track { display: block; height: 12px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--surface-2); overflow: hidden; }
  .playground .sp-fill { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 6px; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .playground .sp-bar { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
